---
import CafeCalculator from '../../components/CafeCalculator.astro';
---

<CafeCalculator lang="en">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>How it is calculated</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cost per cup</strong> = coffee (price per kg × grams) + milk (price per liter × ml) + cup, lid, sugar and other extras.</li>
      <li><strong>Margin per cup</strong> = net selling price − cost per cup.</li>
      <li><strong>Cost percentage</strong> = cost ÷ net selling price × 100. For drinks, the usual target is <strong>20–30%</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Suggested price:</strong> the selling price including tax that hits your target cost percentage.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How to lower your costs</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Use a scale:</strong> weighing every shot saves coffee gram by gram and keeps taste consistent.</li>
      <li><strong>Waste less milk:</strong> use the right pitcher size and don't keep reheating leftover milk.</li>
      <li><strong>Negotiate with your roaster:</strong> ask for a volume discount on regular orders.</li>
      <li><strong>Keep the menu short:</strong> fewer items mean less stock going off.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The full guide: <a href="/en/how-to-open-a-coffee-shop/">How to open a coffee shop: equipment list and costs</a>.</p>
  </div>
</CafeCalculator>
